ntent": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}]}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "type": "DWS", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "engenn9le17ob05re7pdf01.pdf"}]}]}], "template_override": 1, "id": 11, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nListen to an early rock and roll song.\n"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "\nInstructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment.\n"}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn9le17ob05re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le17ob05re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn9le17ob05re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn9le17ob05re2img01.jpg", "text": "You must have heard the names Chuck Berry, Elvis Presley, and the Beatles before! Did you realize they had something in common? If you had answered that they are four of the greatest rock and roll acts ever, then you would have been right. If it hadn't been for these artists, and the music they created, music wouldn't have been the same.", "id": 1}, {"time": "20000", "image": "engenn9le17ob05re2img02.jpg", "text": "If there hadn't been any African-American rhythm and blues artists, rock and roll would never have been born. In the early 1950s, singers like Chuck Berry and \"Fats\" Domino got radio attention. We've listened to singers and songwriters who've been influenced by them ever since. <br /><br />American teenagers were drawn to the driving dance rhythms, lyrics, and its messages. Teens could have just been happy that their parents disapproved at first. They might have enjoyed playing music the older generation hated. Whatever the reason, it caught on and it has held on. If it hadn't, we could have been be listening to Bach!", "id": 2}, {"time": "62000", "image": "engenn9le17ob05re2img03.jpg", "text": "Music producers quickly marketed the new musical style. You might have known that Elvis quickly became rock and roll's first superstar. He became the king of rock and roll almost overnight. Even today, almost 50 years after his death, he has still got that title in his grasp.<br /><br />You may not know that the British beat swept into North America in the 60's. It changed the industry once again. Music for the young has changed many times since then. If your generation hadn't had their own music, what could they have listened to?", "id": 3}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}, {"contents": [{"type": "p", "value": "Queen fans must have been very impressed when they heard that Freddie Mercury had been strongly  influenced by classical music. They might have been pretty astonished and excited  when they heard <span class =\"italic\">Bohemian Rhapsody</span>  and compared it with an opera! In fact, it swept into North America and it wasn't even expected! "}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "text", "id": 2, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The World of Entertainment"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Rock and Roll"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 17}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe situations in spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le17ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "blues"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a type of slow sad music with strong rhythms, developed by African American musicians in the southern US"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If there hadn't been any African-American rhythm and blues artists, rock and roll would never have been born."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when talking about rock and roll."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to disapprove"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200bfeel that something or someone is \u200bbad, \u200bwrong, etc."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Teens could have just been happy that their parents disapproved at first. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob05aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "grasp"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200bquickly take something in \u200byour hand(s) and \u200bhold it \u200bfirmly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Even today, almost 50 years after his death, he has still got that title in his grasp. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob05aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to sweep"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to move quickly and/or smoothly, especially in a way that impresses or is intended to impress other people"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You may not know that the British beat swept into North America in the 60's."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob05aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online or to the library and find a song and lyrics sung by Chuck Berry or Elvis Presley."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen to the song without looking at the lyrics, and see how much you can write down by listening to it 3 or 4 times."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Now take the lyrics and compare it to what you have written."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Highlight mistakes, note words that you have left out, and correct then."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen again with the complete lyrics sheet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take your song to class and read the lyrics to a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss what you think the song is about and anything that might be unclear."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I listen to a song sung by Chuck Berry or Elvis Presley."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write down the lyrics as I listen. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I compare what I have written to the lyrics sheet."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make corrections and note words I have missed."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I take my lyrics to class and share them with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss the meaning of the song and any unclear ideas init with a partner."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Talking Hypothetically about the Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">could have </span> and <span class=\"strong\">would have</span> to talk about things that were possible in the past and may or may not have happened.<br/> You often use these structures with the third conditional. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" modal\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"could\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"done\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"would\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"said\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">could have </span> to talk about possibilities if something had been different in the past. <br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">If it hadn't, we <span class=\"strong\">could have been </span> listening to Bach!</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">would have </span> to imagine a result if something had been different in the past. <br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">If you had answered that they are four of the greatest rock and roll acts ever, then you <span class=\"strong\">would have been </span> right.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would have</span>  expresses more certainty about the result than <span class=\"strong\">could have.</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the third conditional:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Conditional Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Third\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" If + Past Perfect, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">could/would have</span>  + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">If </span> your generation <span class=\\\"strong\\\">hadn't had </span> their own music, what <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could they have listened </span> to?</span> \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you had answered that they are four of the greatest rock and roll acts ever, then you would have been right."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If it hadn't been for these artists, and the music they created, music wouldn't have been the same."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If it hadn't, we could have been be listening to Bach!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If your generation hadn't had their own music, what could they have listened to? "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Speculation About the Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">modals</span> to talk about degrees of certainty and speculate about things in the past.<br/> You use them to describe what is definite, probable, possible, or impossible from the speaker's point of view. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">must</span> , <span class=\"strong\">may</span> , <span class=\"strong\">might</span> , and <span class=\"strong\">could</span>  to describe degrees of certainty.<br/> You can use modals with the<span class=\"strong\"> Present Perfect </span> to talk about the possibility of a past event that is not clear in the present context."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">must have heard </span> the names Chuck Berry, Elvis Presley, and the Beatles before!</span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart for the meanings of modals when speculating about the past:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Modal Phrase\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Must have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It is very likely\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"May have  <br/> Might have <br/> Could have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It is possible \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>May have has a slightly stronger meaning that might have or could have.</li><li>You can add <span class=\"strong\">not </span> to make a negative speculation (It <span class=\"strong\">may not have been</span>  true).</li> </ul></span> "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You may not know that the British beat swept into North America in the 60's. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You might have known that Elvis quickly became rock and roll's first superstar."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Teens could have just been happy that their parents disapproved at first."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They might have enjoyed playing music the older generation hated. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "driving"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "strong and powerful; having a strong influence in making something happen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: American teenagers were drawn to the driving dance rhythms, lyrics, and its messages. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob05aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to influence"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to have an effect on the way that somebody behaves or thinks, especially by giving them an example to follow"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We've listened to singers and songwriters who've been influenced by them ever since."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rock and roll"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a \u200bstyle of \u200bpopular \u200bdance \u200bmusic that \u200bbegan in the 1950s in the US and has a \u200bstrong, \u200bloud \u200bbeat and \u200bsimple \u200brepeated \u200btunes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If there hadn't been any African-American rhythm and blues artists, rock and roll would never have been born."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le17ob05aud02"}]}]}